Package scope
-------------

The workspace's default Cargo license applies to original code. The public
iso-types, iso-types-macros, and iso-types-locations packages retain a combined
SPDX expression covering original code and data. In that expression, OR offers
a choice for the original code; AND preserves the additional data licenses.
The source attributions below identify the materials covered by each license.

iso-types contains the selected catalogs, English Fluent resources, and regional
metadata. iso-types-macros contains the catalog selection index and locale scope
derived from the same inputs. iso-types-locations contains the selected UNECE
directory and uses iso-types for country and subdivision types.

The unpublished iso-types-locale-consumer, iso-types-icu-data, web, and xtask
packages inherit the original-code license. Their dependencies and data retain
their respective licenses. The flag assets under web/public/assets/flags carry
the HatScripts MIT notice in that directory's LICENSE.md. Cargo.lock records the
dependency versions; each dependency supplies its own license and notices.

Redistribution
--------------

Preserve the applicable copyright notices, license texts, and source attributions
when redistributing covered materials. For LGPL-covered materials in distributed
binaries, follow LICENSE-LGPL-2.1 sections 4-6, including covered source
availability and the applicable relinking and customer modification requirements.
For CC-BY-4.0 materials, preserve attribution, provide the license reference, and
identify modifications as described in LICENSE-CC-BY-4.0. These requirements also
apply when covered materials are included in a proprietary application.

Root NOTICE and LICENSE-* files are authoritative. python3 -m tools.codegen
copies them into each public crate; python3 -m tools.codegen --check verifies
the copies. Complete upstream inputs and their provenance live in this repository:
https://github.com/stayhydated/iso-types

Third-party data
----------------

The ISO source snapshots in data/iso/iso_*.json (except
iso_finite.json), the generated ISO tables and ISO entries in the macro selection index,
and corresponding English Fluent catalog names derive from iso-codes:
https://salsa.debian.org/iso-codes-team/iso-codes

Copyright 2016 Dr. Tobias Quathamer <toddy@debian.org>
SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-or-later

The source revision and SHA-256 checksums are recorded in data/iso/provenance.json.
The original source data, editable FTL, and generator are provided in this
repository. The LGPL license text accompanies the public Cargo packages.

English ICU-owned names and currency formatting metadata in data/icu/english.json
and generated catalog tables derive from ICU4X compiled data. Provider versions
and the English display locale are recorded in data/icu/english.json; Cargo.lock
pins provider data packages and checksums.
https://github.com/unicode-org/icu4x
Copyright Unicode, Inc.
SPDX-License-Identifier: Unicode-3.0
The Unicode license text accompanies the public Cargo packages.

Current-data selection uses CLDR coverage, script, validity, alias, and currency
metadata under the Unicode license, plus current ISO 4217 code facts published
by SIX. Retrieval dates, releases, URLs, and checksums are recorded in
data/current/provenance.json in the repository.

Common measurement-unit identifiers, categories, and English display names derive
from CLDR validity data and the English locale. The complete pinned upstream inputs
and checksums are provided under data/current; generated Cargo packages contain
the selected catalog. ICU4X compiled conversion data supplies conversion factors,
temperature offsets, and reciprocal rules when unit-conversion is enabled.

Regional preferences, language/script relationships, and ranked/mixed-unit
preferences derive from pinned CLDR supplemental data under Unicode-3.0.
Geographic relationships use numerical classification facts from the UN
Statistics Division M49 overview, retrieved on the date recorded in provenance:
https://unstats.un.org/unsd/methodology/m49/overview/

IANA location identifiers and country associations derive from zone.tab and
zone1970.tab in the IANA Time Zone Database. These tables are in the public domain.
https://www.iana.org/time-zones
The revision and checksums are recorded in data/current/provenance.json.
Jiff supplies transition rules through its bundled database dependency.

Telephone prefixes derive from libphonenumber's PhoneNumberMetadata.xml.
Postal schemas derive from libaddressinput metadata and RegionDataConstants.java.
https://github.com/google/libphonenumber
https://github.com/google/libaddressinput
Copyright Google Inc.
